Chapter: EncodeGltfBounds
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Encode chapter Gltf

 glTF 2.0 section 5.1: an accessor's min and max are the componentwise
 bounds of the data the accessor describes, in the same units. The
 validator compares them against the buffer, and renderers frame the
 camera and cull with them, so a bound in the wrong units loads and draws
 with a volume the wrong size rather than failing loudly.

 This chapter carries positions at fixed-point scale 1000 and the buffer
 writes them divided by 1000, so a vertex at x = 2.0 is held as 2000 and
 the accessor must say 2.0.

 The mesh below reaches 2.0 on x and -0.5 on y deliberately. A mesh at the
 origin would have min [0,0,0], which is the one bound that reads correctly
 whether or not the scale is applied, so an origin-only probe passes
 against the defect this pins.

Section: Body

  v0 : GltfVertex = gltf-vertex 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
  v1 : GltfVertex = gltf-vertex 2000 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
  v2 : GltfVertex = gltf-vertex 0 (0 - 500) 1500 0 0 0 0 0

  tri : GltfMesh = gltf-mesh [v0, v1, v2] [0, 1, 2]

  json : Text = gltf-build-json tri 0

 A substring search rather than a full-document compare: the assertion is
 about the two bounds, and pinning the whole document would go red for any
 unrelated field and hide which one moved.

  has : Text -> Text
  has (needle) = if text-contains json needle then "present" else "ABSENT"

  r : Text, Text -> Text
  r (what) (got) = "  " & what & " " & got

Section: Report

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "Accessor bounds, which must be the real coordinates and not"
    print-line-uni "the scale-1000 integers the mesh carries:"
    print-line-uni (r "min [0,-0.5,0]  " (has "\"min\":[0.000,-0.500,0.000]"))
    print-line-uni (r "max [2,0,1.5]   " (has "\"max\":[2.000,0.000,1.500]"))
    print-line-uni ""
    print-line-uni "The defect this replaced emitted the raw fixed-point value, so"
    print-line-uni "these must NOT appear:"
    print-line-uni (r "raw min       " (has "\"min\":[0,-500,0]"))
    print-line-uni (r "raw max       " (has "\"max\":[2000,0,1500]"))
    print-line-uni ""
    print-line-uni "Controls. Counts and indices are genuine integers and must stay"
    print-line-uni "integers, so the decimal must not have leaked into them:"
    print-line-uni (r "count 3       " (has "\"count\":3"))
    print-line-uni (r "componentType " (has "\"componentType\":5126"))
    print-line-uni (r "asset version " (has "\"version\":\"2.0\""))
  end

